The pointer `vnet_hdr` pointed directly into the mmap'd TX ring buffer shared with userspace. The kernel validated the header via `__packet_snd_vnet_parse()` but later re-read all fields from the same shared memory in `virtio_net_hdr_to_skb()`, allowing a concurrent userspace thread to modify the header fields between validation and use, bypassing all safety checks (TOCTOU race).

